00:35:37.060 --> 00:35:38.650
For now, we'll just
send it to email.

00:35:38.650 --> 00:35:41.661
Again, I could add some docs.

00:35:41.661 --> 00:35:43.160
I don't really know
what to do here.

00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:46.870
Maybe this is, send an email
to someone to let them know.

00:35:46.870 --> 00:35:48.220
Who knows?

00:35:48.220 --> 00:35:53.580
And we'll call this database
over quota threshold.

00:35:53.580 --> 00:35:54.720
And we'll save that policy.

00:35:57.710 --> 00:35:58.710
And we'll go back.

00:35:58.710 --> 00:35:59.210
Cool.

00:35:59.210 --> 00:36:01.450
We have that policy,
and you can see.

00:36:01.450 --> 00:36:03.200
I have not unfortunately
found a great way

00:36:03.200 --> 00:36:06.189
to start triggering these,
because obviously it

00:36:06.189 --> 00:36:06.980
takes a little bit.

00:36:06.980 --> 00:36:11.550
And for instance, storage
isn't monetized immediately.

00:36:11.550 --> 00:36:13.120
But you have to trust me--

00:36:13.120 --> 00:36:14.660
I get these emails all the time.

00:36:14.660 --> 00:36:17.610
They're fantastic.

00:36:17.610 --> 00:36:19.340
I will show one other thing.

00:36:19.340 --> 00:36:23.270
I will pop over to
the Billing tab.

00:36:23.270 --> 00:36:32.110
And I don't actually
know if I can do that.

00:36:32.110 --> 00:36:35.120
I'll switch projects
and show you a billing

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:36.770
account in a different project.

00:36:45.100 --> 00:36:48.104
I like how it shows it and
then immediately-- there we go.

00:36:48.104 --> 00:36:49.770
So I do have a billing
account for here,

00:36:49.770 --> 00:36:51.900
and I will show
you billing alerts.

00:36:51.900 --> 00:36:54.450
So go to the Linked
Billing Account.

00:36:54.450 --> 00:36:59.340
So I can set up a budget that
is my $50 a month spend limit.

00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:05.260
And you can see that trigger
alerts at 50%, 90%, and 100%.

00:37:05.260 --> 00:37:11.990
And you can see there that
I've used $7.68 out of $10.

00:37:11.990 --> 00:37:14.670
Oh, I ramped it down.

00:37:14.670 --> 00:37:16.620
We'll actually call
that a $10 a month

00:37:16.620 --> 00:37:19.170
spending limit
linked to a project.

00:37:19.170 --> 00:37:21.930
I can say, hey, target it to
last month's spend and let me

00:37:21.930 --> 00:37:24.030
know if I'm above
last month's spend,

00:37:24.030 --> 00:37:26.520
which was I guess $10.60.

00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:30.730
Or I could enter maybe I'm going
to bump it up and call it $15.

00:37:30.730 --> 00:37:32.030
Note how it autocalculates too.

00:37:32.030 --> 00:37:34.040
So I can add just a percent.

00:37:34.040 --> 00:37:37.380
Maybe notify me at
150% of my budget

00:37:37.380 --> 00:37:39.690
just in case I keep going over.

00:37:39.690 --> 00:37:42.660
And as John mentioned,
you can connect this up

00:37:42.660 --> 00:37:43.720
to a Pub/Sub topic.

00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:45.960
You can get fed
into Functions so

00:37:45.960 --> 00:37:48.090
that you can start
turning resources off

00:37:48.090 --> 00:37:49.180
or to other things.

00:37:49.180 --> 00:37:51.360
So we'll save it.

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:55.440
And if I set it below
I could get an email

00:37:55.440 --> 00:37:57.020
and prove it to you there.

00:37:57.020 --> 00:37:59.310
But you won't do that.

00:37:59.310 --> 00:38:02.100
Nope, other way.

00:38:02.100 --> 00:38:02.820
Back to slides.

00:38:02.820 --> 00:38:06.090
So John talked
about Firebase being

00:38:06.090 --> 00:38:09.900
ready organizationally and
from a legal and compliance

00:38:09.900 --> 00:38:10.740
standpoint.

00:38:10.740 --> 00:38:14.220
And then I talked about
productionization, scaling,

00:38:14.220 --> 00:38:17.820
monitoring, alerting,
understanding the finances

00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:19.050
of your application.

00:38:19.050 --> 00:38:22.290
So yes, at this point
we believe that Firebase

00:38:22.290 --> 00:38:24.990
is ready for the needs
of large organizations.

00:38:24.990 --> 00:38:26.311
There's still a lot to work on.

00:38:26.311 --> 00:38:28.560
But as we integrate deeper
with Google Cloud Platform,

00:38:28.560 --> 00:38:31.920
we'll keep getting more of the
compliance, more regionality,

00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:35.430
more awesome monitoring and
scaling and budgeting alerting

00:38:35.430 --> 00:38:37.300
through Google Cloud.

00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:39.380
So thank you,
everyone, for coming.

00:38:39.380 --> 00:38:42.080
We'll be around after for
questions, if you have them.

00:38:42.080 --> 00:38:44.050
